en xx  	                                   plants about a cubit longxx  	               2 months passxx  	     4. c\a-—o —o la ve  (SV)         panicle-bearing shoots bud forthxx  	               2 weeks passxx  	     5. \ø-nu q\ø÷ p\e÷ t»ø÷ la ve  (SV)  the panicles pop forth from the heads of xx  	                                      the shootsxx  	               andxx  	     6. phï qhø ph\‰÷ ve  (SV)      "[plants] come into the gray [phase]": the xx  	                                   flowers (\ø-v»e÷) and kernels (\ø-«s—î) appear, xx  	                                   and the whole field looks grayxx  	               a week or two passxx  	     7. \ø-nu ø la ve  (SV)         the panicles bend [under their own weight, xx  	                                   as the rice grains (c\a-qha) grow big]xx  	               two or three weeks passxx  	     8. c\a m‰ ve  (SV)             the paddy ripens (turning yellow).hw 	c\apos 	Vadjgl  	be *clever, *skillful; be *strong, *active, *energetic; be *brave; be *diligent, *industriousnote	cf. ch\˙(n) (V)ex  	≥\a m|a \o, m|a c\a qo, \a-p—u qh»‰ t\‰÷ ve Ÿg\a÷-y\u a ni exgl	O.K., son-in-law, if you're so smart, just try to catch this fart of mine!ex  	y»ø k|an te c\a j»a exgl	He's a very good worker.ex  	hø chi t»e kh‰ c\a j»a exgl	This elephant is a strong worker.note	see homophonous sentence under next entry.hw 	c\a(n)pos 	Vadjloan	LOANgl  	be *fierce; *dangerous; *rough; *violentnote	< Shan kyam [Cu 77-8]; SYN. h\ay (Vadj)..hw 	hø chi t»e kh‰ c\a(n) j»a /      This elephant is very vicious.xx  	     hø chi t»e kh‰ c\a(n) j»a /      This elephant is very vicious...hw 	chø-c\a-chø-l»ø  pos 	Elabngl  	vicious people..hw 	n»e-c\a-n»e-l»ø  pos 	Elabngl  	fierce demons.hw 	c\apos 	Clfloan	LOANgl  	for *shelve|s; *layer|s; *level|s; *section|snote	< Tai (cf. Shan s»an [Cu 165], Si. ch|an); cf. t»o÷ (Clf), t»ø÷ (Clf)..hw 	th—î n»î c\a  pos 	NPqgl  	two shelves