ing nickname)ngl 	b. a *mute man (incapable of speech)note	cf. q—a (Vadj)..hw 	c\a-qu  pos 	Ngl  	name of the to-bo [q.v.] of a RL village visited in 1977..hw 	c\a=qu-n|î  pos 	Ngl  	["Redskin": nickname]note	cf. ni ± n|î (Mpfx; Bn) 'sthg red; sthg naked', Ÿg»a÷=q|u-ni (N) 'kind of mangy-looking tailless chicken without breast-feathers'..hw 	c\a-q|u-n»‰÷  pos 	Ngl  	nickname of Th»u-y\înote	see Frontispiece photo..hw 	c\a-q|‰  pos 	Ngl  	[jocular or insulting nickname]note	cf. perhaps q|‰ \‰ (AEstat) 'stupidly grinning'..hw 	c\a-q|ay  pos 	Ngl  	nickname of a man who had a double finger (in Hw\e-v|ay [q.v.])note	cf. l\a÷-nø=q|ay (N)..hw 	c\a-kh»a-n|î  pos 	Ngl  	[cf. kh»a (Bn; Belab) 'gold' and n|î (Bn) 'red']..hw 	c\a-khï  pos 	Ngl  	name given to boy born on a moonlit night or at midnightnote	cf. khï (Bn); this is YP's real name [cf. y»a-p—a=|‰ (N)]..hw 	c\a-kh—ï  pos 	Ngl  	[< Shan khüin 'ascend; increase' [Cu 132]; cf. Si. kh»yn]..hw 	c\a-g»‰  pos 	Ngl  	[cf. g»‰ (N) 'spear']..hw 	c\a=co-«s|ï  pos 	Ngl  	[last 2 sylls. prob. 'new life']note	cf. co (Clf; Belab) and «s|ï (N; Mpfx)..hw 	c\a-c|ø  ±  c\a=c|ø-n»‰÷  pos 	Ngl  	["Skinny": nickname]..hw 	c\a-chu=p—a  pos 	Ngl  	["Fatty"; "Fatso": nickname]..hw 	c\a-chï  pos 	Ngl  	[cf. chï (N) 'barking deer']note	this animal has been euphemistically substituted for «s—ï in the cycle; cf. c\a-«s—ï (N)..hw 	c\a-t—î  pos 	Ngl  	name given to an only sonnote	prob. & t|î (Puniv) 'only' and t»e (Num) 'one'; cf. chø-t—î (N)..hw 	c\a-t\î÷  pos 	Ngl  	one of the couple created by Ÿg\ï-«sa after the death of c\a-n»u-c\a-p‰ [q.v.]; "Adam"note	cf. na-t\î÷ (N)..hw 	c\a-t|ø  pos 	Ngl  	[etym.?]..hw 	c\a-th»î  pos 	Ngl  	[cf. th»î (V) 'to dawn, be daybreak']..hw 	c\a-th»ø  pos 	Ngl  	[cf. th»ø-l\a (N) 'rabbit']note	Lahu name of an urbanized Chin man who spoke fluent Lahu and was one of the most knowledgeable guides to the hill villages of N. Thailand; see Frontispiece ph